WEBVTT

00:06.430 --> 00:08.360
There is no need to be afraid.

00:09.860 --> 00:12.400
Once your memories of magic are gone,

00:12.400 --> 00:14.960
even that fear will be 
a thing of the past.

00:15.590 --> 00:18.330
You will merely become an Outsider.

00:18.330 --> 00:22.630
We told you it's not what you think! 
Why won't you listen?!

00:23.080 --> 00:24.410
No...

00:24.410 --> 00:25.640
Please, no!

00:43.170 --> 00:44.440
What is this?

00:44.440 --> 00:46.360
Serpent's Bed of Sand?

00:46.750 --> 00:49.320
They're trying to explain things to you!

00:49.320 --> 00:51.570
It's awful that you won't listen!

00:52.250 --> 00:53.570
Who are they?

00:54.040 --> 00:55.310
They're children.

00:55.950 --> 00:57.830
They burned the pennants.

00:59.650 --> 01:00.960
I really...

01:01.420 --> 01:07.290
hate adults who think children are 
inhuman creatures called "children."

01:07.710 --> 01:10.220
The circumstances of 
the situation don't matter.

01:10.940 --> 01:13.450
The law has been broken.

01:14.550 --> 01:17.010
Peace and order in this world

01:17.010 --> 01:22.000
are maintained only because 
witches strictly adhere to the law.

01:22.810 --> 01:25.730
A single crack in the wall 
brings instant collapse.

01:25.730 --> 01:29.230
No exceptions can be made.

01:29.740 --> 01:34.300
You've talked a lot for someone 
who so adamantly refuses to listen.

01:37.070 --> 01:41.000
Please do not touch my 
apprentices, Easthies.

01:41.840 --> 01:45.380
I see. So they're <i>your</i> students.

01:46.160 --> 01:49.000
They're just as insolent as their master.

01:50.260 --> 01:53.630
If a "good student" would be someone 
like you, then I'm glad they are.

01:54.910 --> 01:58.130
That goes double if this is 
how the Knights Moralis work.

02:00.090 --> 02:03.140
We merely wish to protect order.

02:04.540 --> 02:08.200
Spells powerful enough 
to change the terrain itself—

02:08.200 --> 02:11.050
as in the Dadah Range or the 
Shadow Forest of Thristas—

02:11.050 --> 02:14.050
are spells of war that 
predate the Day of the Pact.

02:15.250 --> 02:21.660
Usage of them, such as this, 
must be dealt with accordingly.

02:21.660 --> 02:22.980
Even so,

02:22.980 --> 02:26.420
it's wrong to take someone's memory 
without even asking the circumstances.

02:26.880 --> 02:31.610
And I've never given my apprentices 
the technique or tools

02:31.610 --> 02:34.180
to complete a spell of this scale.

02:34.980 --> 02:39.310
Even if you didn't, is it possible 
the Brimmed Caps did?

02:44.570 --> 02:46.360
Hey, you two!

02:46.810 --> 02:49.300
A healthy debate's all well and good,

02:49.300 --> 02:52.690
but I hope you haven't forgotten 
what witches are for:

02:53.050 --> 02:55.200
spreading the blessings of magic to all.

02:55.630 --> 02:58.700
Looks like the girls have 
that down better than you.

03:01.290 --> 03:04.620
So quit floating around and help!

03:04.620 --> 03:06.950
Those pennants look like 
they could do a little good!

03:15.140 --> 03:17.440
W-Will that heal him?

03:17.440 --> 03:19.960
No, it's only stopped the bleeding.

03:19.960 --> 03:22.200
I'll take him to Kalhn.

03:22.200 --> 03:25.310
If we can get him to a 
doctor soon, he should pull—

03:25.310 --> 03:26.580
I saw it.

03:26.580 --> 03:29.340
I saw you fix your pennants with magic!

03:30.720 --> 03:33.140
You can fix his wounds, too, can't you?!

03:33.140 --> 03:36.020
Magic has to be capable of that!

03:37.630 --> 03:39.910
No, it is not.

03:40.450 --> 03:43.480
No! That can't be true!

03:43.480 --> 03:44.920
Release me.

03:48.320 --> 03:50.940
Or would you rather I leave him here?

03:56.080 --> 03:57.340
Fine.

03:58.990 --> 04:01.820
Look after him for me.

04:03.710 --> 04:07.560
Let's seal off the site to 
keep all non-witches out.

04:08.690 --> 04:14.210
Once the Outsiders are gone, 
we'll resume the investigation.

05:49.540 --> 05:53.790
<b>The Misgivings of the Knights Moralis</b>

05:57.780 --> 06:00.500
A completely unremarkable basic spell.

06:00.930 --> 06:04.450
She's clearly incapable of destroying 
the land all up and down a river.

06:04.450 --> 06:05.760
Agreed.

06:08.320 --> 06:09.390
Show me your hands.

06:11.440 --> 06:16.450
The Brimmed Caps sometimes 
tattoo seals onto themselves.

06:16.900 --> 06:19.410
Forbidden spells to enhance 
or alter the physical form,

06:19.410 --> 06:22.720
or make their casting more powerful...

06:25.460 --> 06:29.450
<i>Hands stained with ink,
and the calluses of a beginner...</i>

06:37.040 --> 06:39.040
I think you've seen enough.

06:43.810 --> 06:48.180
I'm going to report this to the 
Great Hall and open an investigation.

06:48.540 --> 06:52.000
If your atelier does prove to be 
the source of the problem,

06:52.000 --> 06:53.680
I won't show any mercy.

06:54.070 --> 06:58.310
Take care that you do not lose 
what you've only begun to learn.

07:07.040 --> 07:09.320
What a close call!

07:09.320 --> 07:11.700
I'm glad we all made 
it through unscathed.

07:15.330 --> 07:18.420
I guess we shouldn't have 
left you girls behind.

07:18.420 --> 07:19.870
I really am sorry!

07:19.870 --> 07:22.460
It's not your fault, Master!

07:22.460 --> 07:25.280
Still, Agott, Coco...

07:22.460 --> 07:24.670
Good thing we all came, huh?

07:27.120 --> 07:30.460
I want you to recognize that what 
you did was extremely dangerous.

07:31.070 --> 07:33.970
If anyone were to learn 
the secrets of magic,

07:34.610 --> 07:38.650
all the people we saved would 
have had their memories erased.

07:39.470 --> 07:42.040
Memories are what make up a person's life.

07:42.040 --> 07:45.240
Your actions nearly robbed 
them of a portion of that.

07:45.680 --> 07:47.140
I'm sorry.

07:47.140 --> 07:48.630
I'll be more careful.

07:49.830 --> 07:54.370
<i>I guess I won't be taking 
that test for a while.</i>

07:54.730 --> 07:58.510
But you still made it through. 
Therefore...

07:58.870 --> 08:02.620
I'll arrange for you to take 
the second test, Agott.

08:04.350 --> 08:09.010
If you pass, you'll be qualified to 
accompany me on outside work.

08:10.480 --> 08:14.260
Can you promise not to use magic 
in front of people until then?

08:15.890 --> 08:17.140
Yes!

08:17.140 --> 08:19.510
Aw, just Agott?!

08:19.510 --> 08:22.150
Master, what about us?!

08:22.150 --> 08:26.470
You haven't completed the 
Basics of Casting Primer, remember?

08:27.580 --> 08:30.460
Fine. I hate tests anyway.

08:30.460 --> 08:32.620
There are more tests?!

08:33.800 --> 08:35.500
Hey, Qifrey.

08:36.140 --> 08:37.380
You sure about this?

08:37.380 --> 08:40.180
Weren't you worried about 
Agott getting ahead of herself?

08:40.180 --> 08:41.290
Yes.

08:41.290 --> 08:43.290
Good luck, Agott!

08:41.290 --> 08:42.720
But...

08:44.220 --> 08:45.730
That's not what she's doing here.

08:47.300 --> 08:51.300
I think she's earned herself some trust.

08:51.630 --> 08:53.280
You spoil them.

08:53.280 --> 08:56.440
When my students are too hard 
on themselves, I have no choice.

08:57.690 --> 08:59.310
Master Qifrey!

08:59.970 --> 09:02.320
I want to get back and start practicing!

09:02.320 --> 09:03.430
Wait just a minute.

09:09.470 --> 09:12.540
There's one other thing we should do.

09:13.320 --> 09:16.330
Qifrey's new apprentice 
was that girl, right?

09:16.870 --> 09:18.580
If the rumors are true...

09:19.950 --> 09:22.830
Can you prove that they are?

09:22.830 --> 09:27.620
Nah, it's not possible to find 
evidence in that petrified house.

09:29.000 --> 09:32.420
Then we'll have to make her confess.

09:32.420 --> 09:33.340
Look.

09:34.150 --> 09:38.180
That spell dried up the 
entire area downriver.

09:38.720 --> 09:41.060
A single fallen rock 
can bring down the bank,

09:41.060 --> 09:44.580
divert the river's flow, and 
alter the environment beyond.

09:45.550 --> 09:51.330
The once-beautiful scenery, 
once lost, can never be restored.

09:53.480 --> 09:56.270
<i>That girl could be the first rock.</i>

09:56.270 --> 10:01.620
<i>I must pluck her out before 
she gets the chance to fall.</i>

10:06.130 --> 10:08.880
Olruggio's got a special pen.

10:08.880 --> 10:10.940
It's called a Searwire Wand,

10:10.940 --> 10:14.300
and it lets him burn 
Casting Seals into rocks and trees.

10:16.140 --> 10:18.270
Though it's just a stopgap measure.

10:33.670 --> 10:35.870
The river has begun to return, as well.

10:36.230 --> 10:39.020
The rending spell's effects 
must be wearing off.

10:45.520 --> 10:46.360
Coco.

10:52.150 --> 10:53.870
Here, you dropped these.

10:54.760 --> 10:56.450
Be careful.

10:56.450 --> 10:59.520
You don't want to leave
your cap or ink behind.

11:01.320 --> 11:04.570
I'm sorry. And thank you.

11:07.490 --> 11:09.490
Huh? That's odd...

11:11.070 --> 11:13.690
The vial's still totally full.

11:15.790 --> 11:17.950
Is it a magic vial or something?!

11:17.950 --> 11:20.000
Does it continuously refill?!

11:20.000 --> 11:23.090
Coco, do you mind if 
I have a look at that?

11:23.790 --> 11:25.080
Master?

11:37.350 --> 11:40.910
Magic is a lie that fills 
the world with color.

11:42.800 --> 11:45.980
Though these hands may 
draw beautiful spells,

11:45.980 --> 11:49.160
look at how stained with ink they become!

11:51.860 --> 11:53.410
The nature of a lie...

11:55.630 --> 11:58.110
is that they are outed 
with close scrutiny.

12:07.230 --> 12:10.160
How long can the truth remain hidden?

12:15.010 --> 12:16.890
This Conjuring Ink...

12:17.780 --> 12:20.580
This is the pot that Nolnoa 
in Kalhn gave you, right?

12:20.580 --> 12:21.510
Yes.

12:27.600 --> 12:31.720
Olruggio, take the girls back 
to the atelier, would you?

12:31.720 --> 12:32.820
Huh?

12:32.820 --> 12:35.150
So where are you going, then?

12:35.150 --> 12:36.150
Well...

12:37.990 --> 12:41.970
in all the chaos before, 
I never bought Coco a pen.

12:41.970 --> 12:45.330
It's close by, so we'll make 
a stop in Kalhn first.

12:45.330 --> 12:47.880
Mind picking me up 
some Silvernectar Wine?

12:47.880 --> 12:50.460
One bottle of first flush 
and one bottle of aged!

12:50.460 --> 12:52.330
Yes. Excellent!

12:52.960 --> 12:54.120
Sorry.

12:57.070 --> 13:00.530
<i>There's something 
I really have to look into.</i>

13:07.100 --> 13:10.600
Huh? The door's gone!

13:11.070 --> 13:12.850
Oh, drat.

13:13.270 --> 13:15.360
They're closed today.

13:15.360 --> 13:18.610
What?! The whole shop 
disappears when it's closed?!

13:21.930 --> 13:23.370
Mister Qifrey!

13:24.610 --> 13:26.620
And that girl.

13:26.920 --> 13:29.600
Oh, Tartah! Thank goodness.

13:29.600 --> 13:31.620
I have to speak to Mister Nolnoa.

13:31.620 --> 13:34.130
Oh, hang on just a minute.

13:51.620 --> 13:53.590
Go on in.

14:00.450 --> 14:03.150
This is a totally different 
place than before!

14:04.560 --> 14:06.690
Yeah, different doorknobs 
mean different rooms.

14:06.690 --> 14:08.180
Everyone knows that.

14:09.100 --> 14:11.160
Grandpa should be on the third floor.

14:11.160 --> 14:13.630
Thank you. Excuse us.

14:16.960 --> 14:18.390
Wait a minute...

14:19.020 --> 14:21.670
Um, what's your name again?

14:22.250 --> 14:23.310
Coco.

14:23.670 --> 14:24.930
I'm Coco!

14:24.930 --> 14:29.220
Coco, you should get that cut 
on your right leg cleaned up.

14:30.240 --> 14:31.610
Come back with me.

14:31.930 --> 14:34.310
I've got some tranquileaf 
to disinfect it.

14:42.880 --> 14:45.380
<i>So many unfamiliar components!</i>

14:51.200 --> 14:52.450
It's so beautiful!

14:53.160 --> 14:55.710
What are all these glittery powders?

14:55.710 --> 14:57.900
Don't mess with those, please.

14:57.900 --> 14:59.940
I don't want you putting 
them out of order.

15:01.010 --> 15:03.090
They're magic dyes.

15:03.090 --> 15:06.490
You mix them into the ink 
to alter its effects.

15:09.040 --> 15:10.390
Mister Nolnoa.

15:10.740 --> 15:14.390
Qifrey? We're closed today, you know.

15:14.390 --> 15:17.150
I know, but...

15:18.070 --> 15:19.610
Just kidding.

15:19.610 --> 15:22.900
I know just what you're here for.

15:23.480 --> 15:27.530
The Casting Seal drawn 
on those paving tiles, right?

15:28.280 --> 15:31.250
I haven't figured it out yet.

15:31.250 --> 15:34.790
I've tried a spell to 
separate out the magic dyes,

15:35.320 --> 15:38.200
but they're blended together 
quite thoroughly.

15:38.760 --> 15:41.540
Any clues on your end?

15:41.540 --> 15:44.690
Well, I've acquired something.

15:58.240 --> 16:00.300
It looks just like it!

16:00.810 --> 16:04.570
No, that faint blue hue... 
it's identical!

16:06.100 --> 16:08.430
Where did you get—

16:10.900 --> 16:14.830
Wait a minute. Isn't this <i>my</i> vial?

16:15.890 --> 16:17.260
<i>It happened that day.</i>

16:18.200 --> 16:21.920
<i>The Brimmed Cap cast a spell on the vial.</i>

16:24.170 --> 16:25.600
What are you doing?!

16:26.360 --> 16:29.680
You shouldn't draw with 
that ink until I analyze it!

16:30.610 --> 16:32.010
Qifrey!

16:34.220 --> 16:38.560
Hey, what's that one 
that looks like aquamarine?

16:38.910 --> 16:41.560
The big one dangling from the ceiling!

16:41.560 --> 16:44.190
That's azuremoon flower.

16:44.190 --> 16:47.190
Adding it to ink makes 
your spells last longer.

16:49.160 --> 16:54.200
And the sparkly white one in the 
small bottle on the shelf across from it?

16:54.200 --> 16:56.770
Scales from the blushing bride butterfly.

16:56.770 --> 16:59.570
Mixing it in makes 
the casting ink invisible,

16:59.570 --> 17:01.830
so the casting seal's lines can't be seen.

17:01.830 --> 17:03.470
And next to it?

17:03.470 --> 17:06.640
The narrow bottle is 
powdered roaming scallop.

17:06.640 --> 17:10.270
The squat, round one just beyond is 
powdered golden blaze wyrm scale.

17:14.840 --> 17:16.310
It's amazing!

17:16.970 --> 17:19.320
<i>You're</i> amazing, Tartah!

17:19.320 --> 17:23.100
You've memorized the 
names of all these dyes?!

17:23.100 --> 17:24.860
Well, we do have to sell 'em.

17:25.250 --> 17:28.740
You're so lucky. 
You get to live in a magic stationer's!

17:28.740 --> 17:33.240
Just seeing all these shelves 
and bottles sets my heart racing!

17:33.950 --> 17:37.090
I wish <i>I</i> could live here!

17:38.240 --> 17:41.270
It's way better to live in an atelier.

17:41.980 --> 17:45.500
Not sure why a witch would 
say the stuff you say.

17:46.000 --> 17:49.260
You're not an apprentice witch?

17:50.440 --> 17:51.690
I'm...

17:55.260 --> 17:57.970
Hey, what does that red powder do?

17:57.970 --> 17:59.090
Which?

18:00.190 --> 18:02.140
That one! On that shelf!

18:07.150 --> 18:10.400
Between the aquamarine one 
and the rusty brown one!

18:10.400 --> 18:13.400
Just tell me where on the shelf it is!

18:16.070 --> 18:18.960
It's a really bright red... 
It's easy to see, right?

18:28.500 --> 18:31.140
What made that light?

18:31.140 --> 18:33.180
That was scary!

18:33.180 --> 18:34.590
Are you okay?

18:38.800 --> 18:41.830
Oh, thank goodness none 
of the bottles were broken!

18:45.670 --> 18:47.110
This is awful.

18:47.790 --> 18:49.410
It's a disaster!

18:50.420 --> 18:53.770
The labels came off, 
and they're all mixed up...

18:54.240 --> 18:58.870
Grandpa told me not to touch them, 
and now it's all a mess.

18:58.870 --> 19:02.620
I'm sorry. I'll help you put them 
back where they belong!

19:02.930 --> 19:04.980
Do you know what these are?

19:07.270 --> 19:08.880
Which color is which—

19:08.880 --> 19:10.380
I don't know!

19:11.400 --> 19:13.760
B-But earlier...

19:13.760 --> 19:16.760
I remember them based on 
where they are on the shelf.

19:17.060 --> 19:19.260
I can't tell them apart from the color!

19:27.070 --> 19:30.400
I'm sorry. Please leave.

19:30.770 --> 19:31.810
But...

19:34.190 --> 19:35.510
I'm sorry,

19:36.980 --> 19:39.720
but there's nothing you can do to help.

19:40.850 --> 19:43.860
There are things that 
some people just can't do.

19:44.800 --> 19:47.230
With my Silverwash eyes...

19:47.230 --> 19:50.750
No matter how hard I study, 
I'll never become a witch.

19:55.490 --> 19:57.430
See? I warned you!

19:58.870 --> 20:01.050
Qifrey, are you all right?

20:03.810 --> 20:05.150
Qifrey!

20:06.290 --> 20:10.540
For a Casting Seal that small 
to pack a punch like that...

20:12.300 --> 20:16.070
I think it's a twinned bottle spell.

20:16.910 --> 20:20.060
<i>Two vessels sharing the same contents.</i>

20:20.060 --> 20:24.440
<i>There should be a small medal inscribed 
with a Casting Seal in the fluid.</i>

20:25.170 --> 20:27.620
<i>They made Coco use this...</i>

20:28.440 --> 20:32.290
<i>It was still full because they 
refilled it with that mystery additive.</i>

20:33.180 --> 20:36.140
<i>This bottle is a link to them.</i>

20:38.450 --> 20:42.270
At last... At last I have it!

20:42.890 --> 20:44.530
What is all this?

20:45.010 --> 20:47.070
You're saying the ink in that bottle

20:47.070 --> 20:50.300
can unleash power like that 
even from small, scribbled seals?

20:51.840 --> 20:55.020
Something like that shouldn't exist!

20:55.470 --> 20:58.830
I-It's too much for me to handle!

20:58.830 --> 21:00.910
I must inform the Great Hall!

21:00.910 --> 21:01.700
No!

21:02.620 --> 21:06.790
Neither the Knights Moralis nor the 
Great Hall can be allowed to have this.

21:06.790 --> 21:10.670
It's best if nobody even 
realizes that we know.

21:11.090 --> 21:12.880
Qifrey...

21:14.200 --> 21:15.940
What are you saying?

21:17.170 --> 21:18.420
You...

21:19.040 --> 21:22.650
Do you realize what you're saying?!

21:23.490 --> 21:25.460
What are you going to do?

21:25.460 --> 21:28.060
What are you going to do with that ink?!

21:30.630 --> 21:33.310
I'm sorry, Mister Nolnoa.

21:42.540 --> 21:43.450
Coco.

21:45.390 --> 21:46.590
Sorry for the wait.

21:46.990 --> 21:49.230
About that ink of yours...

21:50.100 --> 21:53.620
It looks like he accidentally gave you 
some extremely expensive stuff.

21:54.090 --> 21:57.250
I bought you a bag to 
make up for it. Here.

21:58.860 --> 22:00.760
Thanks so much!

22:14.610 --> 22:15.870
Master.

22:17.150 --> 22:19.900
What is Silverwash?

22:21.030 --> 22:22.650
Silverwash syndrome...

22:22.650 --> 22:24.630
A congenital condition of the eye

22:25.130 --> 22:29.420
that makes you see the 
entire world in silver.

22:30.640 --> 22:33.910
Witches tend to value good eyesight,

22:33.910 --> 22:36.670
so life is probably difficult 
for those with that condition.

22:37.040 --> 22:41.270
One problem with witches is how 
unaccommodating we are of exceptions.

22:44.250 --> 22:45.430
Coco.

22:47.970 --> 22:50.430
Don't look so worried.

22:51.330 --> 22:52.680
You'll be fine.

22:53.090 --> 22:57.730
As long as you're a student at my atelier, 
I'll do everything I can to protect you.

22:58.670 --> 23:01.820
There's nothing for you to worry about.

23:02.910 --> 23:04.060
Nothing at all.

23:07.820 --> 23:09.670
Grandpa.

23:09.670 --> 23:11.090
Sorry about this.

23:11.090 --> 23:15.820
That light earlier startled me, 
and the jars all got knocked down...

23:16.830 --> 23:19.280
Where'd that flash of light 
come from, anyway?

23:19.730 --> 23:21.710
Did Mister Qifrey cast a spell?

23:23.680 --> 23:26.050
What's this? Flash of light?

23:28.370 --> 23:30.490
I don't remember any flash of light.

23:32.080 --> 23:33.630
Grandpa?

23:35.390 --> 23:39.980
Episode 9:

23:35.390 --> 23:39.980
A Nightmare Stained in Black
